    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30042" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mūrĭcātus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>shaped like a purple-fish, pointed</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">folia spinosa, muricatis cacuminibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					20, 23, 99, § 262</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b> (acc. to murex, II. B. 3.), <i>fearful, timid</i>, as if walking over caltrops: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gressus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Fulg. Myth. 1</span></i>
			.</div>
